      "title": "About | Embracing Digital",
      "summary": "About | Embracing Digital Embracing Digital Home Guidance Briefings (EDTW) What changed Interviews (EDT) How others did it Architectural Deep Dives What to do next Learn Digital Transformation Overview Pillars AI, Cyber, Data, Edge, Computing, Comms ODXA Domains &amp; mappings Whitepapers Monthly synthesis Articles Explainers &amp; analysis Lectures (DTA) Learning series Community Community Newsletter Patreon LinkedIn About About Host Sponsors Shop Search About Embracing Digital A platform for leaders navigating uncertainty, AI disruption, and modern transformation architectures. Our Mission Digital transformation is messy—not marketing spin, but real systemic modernization across people, process, technology, and policy. Embracing Digital was created to help leaders cut through noise, identify real value, and architect transformation in a world reshaped by AI. We believe transformation must be architected —not improvised. That belief drives our commitment to help organizations adopt the Open Digital Transformation Architecture (ODXA), build resilient operating models, and unlock value responsibly. What We Provide ODXA Explained Practical insights into the Open Digital Transformation Architecture (ODXA)—an open architectural framework for aligning capabilities, technology, and mission outcomes across five transformation domains. ODXA provides a rigorous framework for navigating broader ecosystems, including government and enterprise sectors. Digital Transformation Architect Tools Frameworks, playbooks, and real examples to help architects design modernization strategies that survive funding cycles, executive turnover, and operational constraints. News & Signals Weekly briefings distinguish hype from reality by applying architectural thinking to evolving tech, regulation, and emerging AI-driven disruption. Voices from the Field Conversations with practitioners across government, industry, and academia—sharing lived experience rather than vendor narratives. Our Princip",
