      "summary": "The Pivot: Reconciling Silos and Grounding Strategy in Reality | Digital Transformation Architect Embracing Digital Home Guidance Briefings (EDTW) What changed Interviews (EDT) How others did it Architectural Deep Dives What to do next Learn Digital Transformation Overview Pillars AI, Cyber, Data, Edge, Computing, Comms ODXA Domains &amp; mappings Whitepapers Monthly canonical synthesis Articles Explainers &amp; analysis Lectures (DTA) Learning series Community Community Newsletter Patreon LinkedIn About About Host Sponsors Shop Search العربية Deutsch English Français Italiano Português 日本語 The Pivot: Reconciling Silos and Grounding Strategy in Reality 2026-02-18 by Dr. Darren Pulsipher Download PDF Table of Contents Introduction Understanding Reconciliation The Importance of Grounding Lessons from Practice: Case Studies and Applications Implications for Leaders and Practitioners Conclusion Learn More Introduction In the era of digital transformation, organizations face the pressing challenge of effectively aligning strategic ambitions with operational realities. This misalignment often leads to wasted resources, delayed initiatives, and a frustrating lack of progress. Simply having a well-crafted strategy is insufficient if it fails to connect with the existing capabilities of an organization. A common pitfall is treating digital transformation as merely a technological shift, ignoring the necessary alignment between various organizational facets—people, processes, and technology. More often than not, different teams within an organization work in silos, leading to isolated efforts that do not complement each other. This disconnection can create a frustrating gap between executive vision and ground-level execution. To bridge this divide, effective reconciliation and grounding processes are essential. These concepts, as discussed in the lecture titled \"The Pivot: Reconciling Silos and Grounding Strategy in Reality,\" serve as foundational pillars for any successful d",
