      "summary": "Digital Domain | O-DXA | GEAR | Embracing Digital Embracing Digital Home Guidance Briefings (EDTW) What changed Interviews (EDT) How others did it Architectural Deep Dives What to do next Learn Digital Transformation Overview Pillars AI, Cyber, Data, Edge, Computing, Comms ODXA Domains &amp; mappings Whitepapers Monthly synthesis Articles Explainers &amp; analysis Lectures (DTA) Learning series Community Community Newsletter Patreon LinkedIn About About Host Sponsors Shop Search Digital Domain Platforms, data, and software foundations of the GEAR Transformation Operating System Application Distributed Information Management Service Management Software Defined Infrastructure Physical Layer Identity Aspect Security Aspect Domain definition The Digital Domain encompasses the software applications, platforms, data architectures, and integration middleware within the O-DXA structural model and GEAR framework. It provides the technological foundation that connects organizational workflows, automates complex business logic, and unlocks data-driven insights across the transformation dimensions. By standardizing digital interfaces and modernizing legacy application stacks, this domain enables interoperability, rapid feature deployment, and secure multi-cloud operations. Key decisions What is our target data architecture and definition framework? How do we implement a Zero Trust security posture? Which services should be centralized versus distributed? How do we manage identity, authentication, and authorization? Common anti-patterns Technical Debt Accumulation (prioritizing short-term speed over stability) Data Islands (isolated data stores that prevent enterprise-wide visibility) Security as an Afterthought (bolting on security after development) Cross-domain dependencies Organizational Domain Process Domain Physical Domain GEAR Integration & Architect's Map The Digital Domain provides the technological infrastructure and data assets that power the GEAR system. FORGE Method",
