      "title": "O-DXA: The Structural Model of GEAR | Embracing Digital",
      "summary": "O-DXA: The Structural Model of GEAR | Embracing Digital Embracing Digital Home Guidance Briefings (EDTW) What changed Interviews (EDT) How others did it Architectural Deep Dives What to do next Learn Digital Transformation Overview Pillars AI, Cyber, Data, Edge, Computing, Comms ODXA Domains &amp; mappings Whitepapers Monthly synthesis Articles Explainers &amp; analysis Lectures (DTA) Learning series Community Community Newsletter Patreon LinkedIn About About Host Sponsors Shop Search O-DXA: The Structural Model The horizontal map of the GEAR Transformation Operating System Strategic Domain Physical Domain Digital Domain Process Domain Organizational Domain What is O-DXA? The Open Digital Transformation Architecture (O-DXA) is the structural domain model within the GEAR framework. It provides an open architectural framework for aligning capabilities, technology, and mission outcomes across five interacting areas of responsibility: Strategic, Organizational, Process, Digital, and Physical domains. By mapping dependencies across these domains, O-DXA prevents fragmented investments and ensures coherent enterprise transformation. The Five Domains Strategic — Intent, policy, outcomes, and root constraints Organizational — Ownership, accountability, structure, and culture Process — Value flow, workflows, governance mechanisms, and execution Digital — Platforms, data, applications, and integration Physical — Edge assets, devices, networks, and real-world constraints The Transformation Operating System O-DXA defines where coordination must hold. When activated by the FORGE practice and viewed through Execution Pillars , it enables architects to manage the Transformation Dimensions (People, Process, Policy, and Technology) at scale. Mission outcomes delivered through integrated digital capabilities Mission Solutions &amp; Capabilities Architectural FORGE: The active process that connects and aligns all transformation pillars Architectural FORGE Find Find: Identify gaps, silo",
