      "summary": "Embracing Digital Transformation Embracing Digital Home Guidance Briefings (EDTW) What changed Interviews (EDT) How others did it Architectural Deep Dives What to do next Learn Digital Transformation Overview Pillars AI, Cyber, Data, Edge, Computing, Comms ODXA Domains &amp; mappings Whitepapers Monthly canonical synthesis Articles Explainers &amp; analysis Lectures (DTA) Learning series Intelligence Community Community Newsletter Patreon LinkedIn About About Host Sponsors Shop Search Skip to content Home Episodes Episode 382: Put the title Right Here Episode 382 Put the title Right Here 2026-09-03 Hosted by Dr. Darren Pulsipher Summary AI is getting more intimate than ever — but what if it could also make us more human? Dr. Darren welcomes Lyle Maxson, founder of **Above**, to explore **reflective AI**, a new class of ambient AI designed to build emotional intelligence, improve self-awareness, and support healthier relationships at work and at home. They unpack the promise and risks of AI, privacy, consent, and why the future of AI strategy should be judged by human outcomes — not just productivity. ## Key Takeaways - **AI strategy is becoming a behavior strategy:** the real measure of success is whether AI improves judgment, communication, and human performance. - **Engagement is not the goal:** tools optimized for stickiness can create dependency, not capability. - **Reflective AI can act like a coach or “Jiminy Cricket”:** offering feedback loops, daily reflections, and intention-setting to help users grow. - **Emotional intelligence matters more than ever:** EQ can be strengthened through intentional practice, self-awareness, and feedback. - **Privacy and consent must be built in from day one:** ambient AI should use strong safeguards, encryption, and clear user control. - **The best AI helps people become more capable, not more dependent:** the goal is to support better relationships, clearer thinking, and stronger self-development. ## Chapters - **00:00** Int",
